        },
        "section": "",
        "image": "",
        "answer": "b",
        "solution": "Locus of point equidistant from a given straight is the perpendicular bisector of the straight line\n∴Gradient of the line ax + by + c = 0\nimplies by = -ax - c\ny = -a/bx - c\nthe gradient (m) = a/b\n∴Gradient of the perpendicular (m) = b/a\nIf P(x,y) is the point intersection of the two lines equation of the perpendicular becomes\ny - y1 = m(x - x1)\ny - y1 = b/a(x - x1)\nay - ay1 = bx - bx1\nay - bx + bx1 - ay1 = 0\nay - bx + b(x1 - y1) = 0\nimplies ay - bx + q",
        "examtype": "utme",
        "examyear": "2006"
