      {
        "id": 443,
        "question": "The nth term of the sequence 3/2, 3, 7, 16, 35, 74 ..... Is",
        "option": {
          "a": "5 . 2\u003Csup\u003En-2\u003C/sup\u003E - n",
          "b": "5 . 2\u003Csup\u003En-2\u003C/sup\u003E  - (n+1) / 2",
          "c": "3 . 2\u003Csup\u003En-2\u003C/sup\u003E ",
          "d": "3/2 n"
        },
        "section": "",
        "image": "",
        "answer": "a",
        "solution": "3/2, 3, 7, 16, 35, 74, ....\nUsing the method of substitution\nWhen n = 1, 5 . 2\u003Csup\u003En-2\u003C/sup\u003E - 1 = 5 . 2\u003Csup\u003E1-2\u003C/sup\u003E - 1\n= 5 x 2\u003Csup\u003E-1\u003C/sup\u003E - 1\n= 5 x 1/2 - 1\n= 5/2 - 1 = 3/2\nWhen n = 1, 5 . 2\u003Csup\u003En-2\u003C/sup\u003E - n\n= 5 . 2\u003Csup\u003E2-2\u003C/sup\u003E - 2\n= 5 x 2\u003Csup\u003E0\u003C/sup\u003E - 2\n= 5 x 1 – 2 = 3\nWhen n = 3, 5 . 2\u003Csup\u003En-2\u003C/sup\u003E - n\n= 5 . 2\u003Csup\u003E3-2\u003C/sup\u003E - 3\n= 5 x 21 - 3\n= 5 x 2 – 3\n= 10 -3 = 7\nWhen n = 4, 5 . 2\u003Csup\u003En-2\u003C/sup\u003E - n\n= 5 . 2\u003Csup\u003E4-2\u003C/sup\u003E - 4\n= 5 x 2\u003Csup\u003E2\u003C/sup\u003E - 4\n= 5 x 4 – 4\n= 20 – 4 = 16\nWhen n = 5, 5 . 2\u003Csup\u003En-2\u003C/sup\u003E - n\n= 5 . 2\u003Csup\u003E5-2\u003C/sup\u003E - 5\n= 5 x 2\u003Csup\u003E3\u003C/sup\u003E - 5\n= 5 x 8 – 5\n= 40 – 5\n= 35\nWhen n = 6, 5 . 2\u003Csup\u003En-2\u003C/sup\u003E - n\n= 5 . 2\u003Csup\u003E6-2\u003C/sup\u003E - 6\n= 5 x 2\u003Csup\u003E4\u003C/sup\u003E - 6\n= 5 x 16 – 6\n= 80 – 6 = 74\n∴ 5 . 2\u003Csup\u003En-2\u003C/sup\u003E - 1 = 3/2, 3, 7, 16, 35, 74",
        "examtype": "utme",
        "examyear": "2007"
      },
