        "answer": "c",
        "solution": "By comparing y = mx + c\n\nwith y = -4x + 2,\n\nthe gradient of y = -4x + 2 is m1 = -4\n\nlet the gradient of the line parallel to the given line be m2,\n\nthen, m2 = m1 = -4\n\n(condition for parallelism)\n\nusing, y - y1 = m2(x - x1)\n\nHence the equation of the parallel line is\n\ny - 3 = -4(x-2)\n\ny - 3 = -4 x + 8\n\ny + 4x = 8 + 3\n\ny + 4x = 11\n\ny + 4x - 11 = 0",
