      {
        "id": 1009,
        "question": "Find the value of x and y in the simultaneous equation: 3x + y = 21; xy = 30",
        "option": {
          "a": "x = 3 or 7, y = 12 or 8",
          "b": "x = 6 or 1, y = 11 or 5",
          "c": " x = 2 or 5, y = 15 or 6",
          "d": " x = 1 or 5, y = 10 or 7"
        },
        "section": "",
        "image": "",
        "answer": "c",
        "solution": "3x + y = 21 ... (i);\n\nxy = 30 ... (ii)\n\nFrom (ii), y = 30/x\n. Putting the value of y in (i), we have\n\n3x + 30/x = 21\n\n⟹ 3x\u003Csup\u003E2\u003C/sup\u003E + 30 = 21x\n\n3x\u003Csup\u003E2\u003C/sup\u003E  - 21x + 30 = 0\n\n3x\u003Csup\u003E2\u003C/sup\u003E  - 15x -6x + 30 = 0\n\n3x(x - 5) - 6(x - 5) = 0\n\n(3x - 6)(x - 5) = 0\n\n3x - 6 = 0 ⟹ x = 2.\n\nx - 5 = 0 ⟹ x = 5.\n\nIf x = 2, y = 30/2 = 15;\n\nIf x = 5, y = 30/5 = 6.",
        "examtype": "utme",
        "examyear": "2019"
      },
