        "solution": "Equation: x\u003Csup\u003E3\u003C/sup\u003E\n - 2x\u003Csup\u003E2\u003C/sup\u003E\n - 5x + 6 = 0.\n\nFirst, bring out a\u003Csub\u003En\u003C/sub\u003E\n which is the coefficient of x\u003Csup\u003E3\u003C/sup\u003E\n = 1.\n\nThen, aa\u003Csub\u003E0\u003C/sub\u003E\n which is the coefficient void of x = 6.\n\nThe factors of aa\u003Csub\u003En\u003C/sub\u003E\n = 1; The factors of aa\u003Csub\u003E0\u003C/sub\u003E\n = 1, 2, 3 and 6.\n\nThe numbers to test for the roots are ±(a\u003Csub\u003En0/sub\u003E/aa\u003Csub\u003En\u003C/sub\u003E)\n. = ±(1,2,3,6).                                              \nTest for +1: 1\u003Csup\u003E3\u003C/sup\n - 2(1\u003Csup\u003E2\u003C/sup\n) - 5(1) + 6 = 1 - 2 - 5 + 6 = 0.\n\nTherefore x = 1 is a root of the equation.\n\nUsing long division method, x\u003Csup\u003E3\u003C/sup−2x\u003Csup\u003E2\u003C/sup−5x+6/(x−1)\n = x\u003Csup\u003E2\u003C/sup - x - 6.\n\nx\u003Csup\u003E2\u003C/sup - x - 6 = (x - 3)(x + 2).\n\nx = -2, 3.\n\n∴\n The roots of the equation = 1, -2 and 3.",
